  What the screenshots are: 18 Google Flights round-trip searches, 1 adult,
  economy — São Paulo and Rio de Janeiro to "Recife · João Pessoa" (both
  destinations at once), January 2027. Three departure dates (18/19/20 Jan) ×
  three trip lengths (7/8/9 nights), for each origin.

  Lowest fare per search (round-trip total, per adult):

  ┌──────────────────┬────────────┬──────────┬──────────┐
  │       Ida        │  7 noites  │ 8 noites │ 9 noites │
  ├──────────────────┼────────────┼──────────┼──────────┤
  │ São Paulo 18 jan │ R$ 1.380 * │ R$ 1.439 │ R$ 1.439 │
  ├──────────────────┼────────────┼──────────┼──────────┤
  │ São Paulo 19 jan │ —          │ R$ 1.439 │ R$ 1.439 │
  ├──────────────────┼────────────┼──────────┼──────────┤
  │ São Paulo 20 jan │ —          │ R$ 1.438 │ R$ 1.438 │
  ├──────────────────┼────────────┼──────────┼──────────┤
  │ Rio 18 jan       │ R$ 1.824   │ R$ 1.848 │ R$ 1.848 │
  ├──────────────────┼────────────┼──────────┼──────────┤
  │ Rio 19 jan       │ —          │ R$ 1.848 │ R$ 1.848 │
  ├──────────────────┼────────────┼──────────┼──────────┤
  │ Rio 20 jan       │ —          │ R$ 1.758 │ R$ 1.758 │
  └──────────────────┴────────────┴──────────┴──────────┘

  (20 Jan → 29 Jan: SP R$ 1.438, Rio R$ 1.740.)

  Three things worth flagging before you decide:

  1. The SP 18→25 Jan search had no "Sem escalas" filter — every other search
     did. That's the only reason R$ 1.380 exists, and it's the only search
     containing a connecting flight (17h55 via Brasília). Compared
     like-for-like, that cell would be higher.
  2. Most cheap fares are "passagens separadas" — two separate tickets sold
     together. If the outbound is delayed, neither airline owes you a rebooking
     on the return.
  3. Some flights land in João Pessoa (JPA), not Recife (REC) — the search
     covered both cities. LATAM's CGH departure and several GOL night flights
     are JPA.

  São Paulo is consistently ~R$ 400 cheaper than Rio on the same dates, and
  departure date barely moves the price (R$ 1.438 vs R$ 1.439) while origin
  moves it a lot.

